WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.779
There are no moms in One Piece and that's
a great thing.

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:10.060
Like, WITH Mothers, One Piece doesn't work,
as crazy as it sounds.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:15.800
And I can't believe I'm saying this, but Crocodile
might actually be Luffy's mother, because

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.849
I've found a lot of new evidence for it.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:26.460
BUT, I also found a number of other very possible
candidates and I'll show you just how important

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.710
Luffy meeting his mother will be to the entire
story.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:37.980
I 
really can't explain it, but Luffy's mother

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.860
is one of those mysteries in One Piece, that
even though they don't seem to matter at all

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.330
for the story right now, I just can't help
but obsess a little about.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:54.260
There is something really weird going on with
mother's in One Piece and I refuse to believe

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.490
that we won't get to know the mother of the
pirate king himself.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:03.930
What's up, my name is Manu, and just like
you I assume, my mom means the world to me.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:08.860
Of course there are exceptions to this, but
generally I think mom's score pretty pretty

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.350
high on the 'things-people-tend-to-love-no-matter-what'
list.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:17.330
And so today I finally have the chance to
talk about something that has bothered me

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.160
for a while now.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.900
You know how Shounen characters all seem to
suffer from bad 'I-have-no-dad' syndrome?

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.740
Well One Piece takes that a step further.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:40.049
Here everyone seems to suffer from 'Wait-what-I-don't-even
-get-a-mom' syndrome as well.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.500
And as it turns out there is actually a reason
for that, that I think is important to discuss

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.260
before getting into Luffy's mom specifically.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:54.210
Okay, how do I put this: There are no mothers
in One Piece.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.610
That's a weirder sentence to say out loud
than I thought it would be.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.270
But it's an undeniable fact.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.750
None of the straw hats has a mother as of
now.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.960
Luffy, Zoro and Jinbe never have mentioned
their parents.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.899
Franky and Chopper got abandoned by theirs.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:14.210
Brook's parents must be dead, because he's
a grandpa.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:23.349
And Robin, Usopp, Sanji and Nami have lost
their mothers under the most tragic circumstances.

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:34.569
And what I just realized is that those four
share very similar arcs.

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:40.090
All their mothers were incredibly kind and
brave people that inherited that kindness

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:47.490
to their child.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:53.020
All of them then had the most terrible and
lonely childhoods after losing their mother,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.410
suffering under a terrible lack of self confidence.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:02.050
And all four of them were the ones that opposed
Luffy out of that sense that they were not

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:15.419
worth anything and in the end under tears
accepted luffy's unconditional love for them.

00:03:15.419 --> 00:03:16.419
[]

00:03:16.419 --> 00:03:42.470
And now that I think about it, you can actually
spin that in the other direction as well.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:48.690
Chopper and Franky are the most quirky members
of the crew, the 'non-normals', not because

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:53.409
they are a cyborg and a reindeer, but because
they were abandoned.

00:03:53.409 --> 00:03:57.370
Only now fitting in with a crew that accepts
them.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.900
And lastly the four members that don't seem
to have a tragic backstory with their moms,

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:06.629
at least yet, are the four emotionally most
stable ones.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:20.680
Luffy, Zoro, Brook and Jinbe I feel share
that aura of stability and groundedness.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:26.220
Now Zoro does clearly have some issues of
his own, that probably relate to growing up

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.210
without parents and always fighting ever since
he was a kid.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.890
I hope we'll get to meet his parents soon.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:36.520
Jinbe's darkness stems from the discrimination
of his people overall.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:45.800
And brook's is spending such a long time alone.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.960
But I find it beyond interesting that there
seems to be a clear pattern connected to mothers

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.960
in the story.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:58.070
And so it was no big surprise to find out
that this lack of motherly care was not an

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.449
accident, but something consciously decided
by author Eiichiro Oda.

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:07.940
As he explained in an SBS, mothers for him
are the opposite of adventure.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:12.600
They take care of their children and protect
them from going on a journey that might well

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.500
cost them their lives.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:21.419
And so you can't have a great pirate adventure
with loving moms around.

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:27.040
Now this statement may sound very trivial,
but when you stop and think about what we

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:33.130
just discussed about the straw hats, Oda took
great care to include the negative implications

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.790
of not having a mom into consideration.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:45.669
The most tragic backstories are related to
losing a mom or being abandoned by one.

00:05:45.669 --> 00:05:52.750
Either bringing out the best or worst in people.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.949
For example Dofi and Corazon.

00:05:54.949 --> 00:05:58.520
And you see it with everyone, Ace, Sabo, Law.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:04.639
Oda knows that mothers are important, but
was smart enough to keep them out of his adventure

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:10.020
story, which will be very important later,
when we will look at the possible candidates

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.290
for Luffy's mom.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:17.360
And wether he was aware of all the fantastic
effects this would have or not as a 20 year

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:24.260
old, I think this decision has contributed
immensely to why One Piece works so well as

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:25.790
a story.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:32.070
Think about it, while you might at first glance
go fully woke and say 'Oda doesn't like women',

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:38.860
in truth loving mothers are something extremely
treasured and rare in this world.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.340
If you have a loving mother you have won the
ultimate jackpot, you can live a happy life

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.639
away from violence and hate.

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:52.250
And so the fact that there literally are no
loving mothers in One Piece, motivates the

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.199
entire story.

00:06:54.199 --> 00:06:55.250
Seriously.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:59.419
All the characters now have motivation and
reason to become pirates.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:05.030
They all have the potential to be saved by
Luffy, because he gives them that unconditional

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.770
love, they are supposed to get from their
moms.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:15.229
As a result, crews like Luffy's or Whitebeards
are the real loving families in One Piece,

00:07:15.229 --> 00:07:22.160
because there are no regular loving ones.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:36.039
And why brotherly bonds like that of Luffy,
Sabo and Ace or that of Noriko and Nami are

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:39.080
more common than having actual siblings.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:46.380
It's why crews like Doflamingo's exist, where
characters like baby five try to find some

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:57.900
twisted sense of love 
and belonging.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:04.580
Or Big Mom's crew, who is a caricature and
dark twist on the concept of a loving mother.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.900
A woman so overly obsessed with creating a
big family for everyone in the world and so

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:15.900
scarred by being *cough cough* abandoned by
her mother caramel, that she ironically lost

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:29.520
sight of her actual children, using them as
tools.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:38.789
As Oda says, real loving Mom's are the opposite
of adventure and pirates.

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:41.430
But I think it goes even further than that.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:45.779
The fact that there are no mothers in One
Piece and all the tragedy that comes with

00:08:45.779 --> 00:08:52.809
it, is in a way the biggest reason why this
world is broken and needs to change.

00:08:52.809 --> 00:08:58.420
A world in which pirate crews and revolutionary
armies and marines are the only family people

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:04.350
can have, many of them emotionally scared,
is a world that needs to change.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:10.339
I strongly believe that the dawn Luffy needs
to bring has to shine on a world where kids

00:09:10.339 --> 00:09:14.870
can grow up in the arms of their mothers,
not having to fight.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.170
Oh wow.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:19.600
I really went deep on this one huh.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:25.410
But I really love how deep one piece always
turns out to be when you dig just little beneath

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.559
the surface.

00:09:26.559 --> 00:09:31.639
Before we get into Luffy's mom now, if you
enjoy these kind of deep dives AND some good

00:09:31.639 --> 00:09:36.800
theories on top, I'd appreciate it immensely
if you considered subscribing to the channel

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.439
for more weekly one piece content like this.

00:09:40.439 --> 00:09:46.561
Okay, so - Luffy's mom: It's difficult to
talk about who and where she might be, because

00:09:46.561 --> 00:09:55.760
Luffy does have a step mom of sorts.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:05.649
Dadan is pretty much Luffy's loving mother
figure, that, while tough, raised him in a

00:10:05.649 --> 00:10:08.410
caring home.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:22.999
And Luffy loves Dadan back like a son, even
if he doesn't see her as a literal mom.

00:10:22.999 --> 00:10:28.260
In a way you could even argue that Luffy might
be so incredibly special in this world BECAUSE

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:34.360
he grew up with a loving, if violent, family
of bandits, his two brothers and garp.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.360
So why do I think that after all that, Luffy
even needs a mom and that we will definitely

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.940
meet her in the story?

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:49.369
Well some of it comes from Oda himself - in
very tiny bites and bits, as always.

00:10:49.369 --> 00:10:54.980
He himself told us that she is still alive
and that he has already drawn her.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:11:00.069
But on top of that, we just discussed that
Oda actually thinks so highly of motherly

00:11:00.069 --> 00:11:04.999
characters and their influence, that he concisely
decided to keep her away from Luffy.

00:11:04.999 --> 00:11:10.819
He described it as Luffy starting his adventure
the moment he left his parents arms.

00:11:10.819 --> 00:11:15.350
What I personally think Oda is hinting at
with this, is that we will only meet Luffy's

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.779
mother at the end of the story.

00:11:17.779 --> 00:11:24.360
Actually, no, WE might ALREADY find out sooner
than Luffy, but Luffy himself will only meet

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:25.889
his mother towards the end.

00:11:25.889 --> 00:11:28.279
When his adventure is over.

00:11:28.279 --> 00:11:32.170
I've talked about this before, but I like
to think that Luffy's adventure ends with

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:38.579
finding the one piece, and that the big war
that must follow after is in a way a separate

00:11:38.579 --> 00:11:40.089
or new story.

00:11:40.089 --> 00:11:45.920
So I to me it would make sense if he met his
mom after reaching laugh tale, but before

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.519
the final big war or showdown.

00:11:48.519 --> 00:11:54.149
I know people really don't like the idea of
the straw hats being special or Luffy being

00:11:54.149 --> 00:11:58.790
the chosen one, because I guess they feel
like it would undermine his achievements.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.759
And I have bad and good news for you.

00:12:01.759 --> 00:12:08.370
Because Luffy is definitely the chosen one,
but that doesn't take away anything from all

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:18.959
he has accomplished.

00:12:18.959 --> 00:12:22.209
Luffy's choices and all he has worked for
matters.

00:12:22.209 --> 00:12:27.720
It's just that being born special, gave him
the chance to reach his full potential int

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.259
he first place.

00:12:29.259 --> 00:12:34.119
But it was up to Luffy to live up to this
potential.

00:12:34.119 --> 00:12:39.079
Same goes for characters like Sanji or Zoro,
who we now know also come from unique and

00:12:39.079 --> 00:12:41.049
special circumstances.

00:12:41.049 --> 00:12:46.369
But because they all have to work hard and
sacrifice a lot to reach the level they are

00:12:46.369 --> 00:13:12.089
at now anyways, I think it doesn't take away
at all from their achievements.

00:13:12.089 --> 00:13:17.379
My point here, is that Luffy, the grandson
of the strongest marines and son of the leader

00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:22.089
of the revolutionary army, definitely will
have a special mother.

00:13:22.089 --> 00:13:23.889
No question about it.

00:13:23.889 --> 00:13:30.329
The only question we now have to answer, and
boy it's a big one, is, who?

00:13:30.329 --> 00:13:31.910
Who is Luffy's mom?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:36.730
So, I now want to run through all the possible
candidates we have so far.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.689
And you might be surprised about the last
character I propose here.

00:13:41.689 --> 00:13:56.540
One of the most popular theories out there
is the forbidden love theory.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:02.079
The idea here, is that Dragon met a celestial
dragon, and after spending more and more time

00:14:02.079 --> 00:14:04.869
together, a romance begins to blossom.

00:14:04.869 --> 00:14:10.259
This would be a classic, bird in the golden
cage scenario, where the woman yearns for

00:14:10.259 --> 00:14:16.920
the same sort of freedom that Dragon enjoys
and at some point they have a baby together.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.879
As the other celstial dragons find out, the
is tortured and ultimately killed for mixing

00:14:21.879 --> 00:14:24.009
royal blood with that of a commoner.

00:14:24.009 --> 00:14:29.749
This, plus all the other knowledge about the
rulers of the world he now has gathered, motivates

00:14:29.749 --> 00:14:32.499
Dragon to form the revolutionary army.

00:14:32.499 --> 00:14:38.059
He hands off Luffy to Garp and dedicates his
life to taking down the world nobles.

00:14:38.059 --> 00:14:41.970
I personally think, this theory is pretty
reasonable and straight forward.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:47.040
It's a classic forbidden love - Romeo and
Juliet sort of approach, that would motivate

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:52.089
dragon, but also give luffy some unique background
that might be important towards the end of

00:14:52.089 --> 00:14:53.089
the story.

00:14:53.089 --> 00:14:57.449
It doesn't blow me away, but it's solid.

00:14:57.449 --> 00:15:03.669
Another candidate is Bello Betty, one of the
commanders of the revolutionary army.

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:09.139
Which seems to fit quite well.

00:15:09.139 --> 00:15:14.629
Betty is the commander of the East Blue, which
is where Luffy grew up and her abilities to

00:15:14.629 --> 00:15:20.829
boost up peoples will and rally them to her
cause is something she shares with our hero.

00:15:20.829 --> 00:15:25.770
On top of that, since Oda mentioned that he
would draw luffs parents in volume 45, people

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:30.459
have been speculating that this woman here
might be Luffy's mom.

00:15:30.459 --> 00:15:34.169
And that might just be an early version of
Betty for all we know.

00:15:34.169 --> 00:15:41.290
This theory does something, no other can,
which is bringing Dragon and his partner close

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.449
together and have them work towards a common
goal.

00:15:44.449 --> 00:15:47.489
It also fits with Oda telling us that she
is still alive.

00:15:47.489 --> 00:15:50.339
I would actually enjoy this one a lot.

00:15:50.339 --> 00:15:56.439
Betty is no regular character, but also not
someone overly famous and mysterious.

00:15:56.439 --> 00:15:59.680
Just someone fighting the government alongside
Dragon.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:00.680
Pretty decent.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:05.589
A very short theory, is that Luffy's mom was
actually Rogers sister.

00:16:05.589 --> 00:16:16.879
That idea is based on the fact that D's seem
to have kids with other Ds.

00:16:16.879 --> 00:16:20.439
That goes for Ace, the only person we know
both parents of.

00:16:20.439 --> 00:16:27.350
But Jaguar D. Saul also mentioned that everyone
in his family was a D. So if it takes two

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:33.059
Ds to make the one who can bring the dawn,
Luffy's mother would also have to be a D.

00:16:33.059 --> 00:16:39.579
This could be true if she was Garps daughter,
but if not, what better family for Luffy to

00:16:39.579 --> 00:16:42.540
have blood from than the Gol family.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:49.610
I like this idea, because it would tie luffy
closer to Roger and Ace, but it also begs

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:53.889
the question why no-one has mentioned Rogers
sister so far.

00:16:53.889 --> 00:16:57.449
Now it's time for one of my favorite candidates
however.

00:16:57.449 --> 00:17:03.299
And that is Jewellery Bonney.

00:17:03.299 --> 00:17:09.339
She is actually a really interesting character
no matter what.

00:17:09.339 --> 00:17:16.329
Because Bonnie's devil fruit allows her to
change her age and presumably that of others.

00:17:16.329 --> 00:17:22.370
Her biggest character trait is her gluttony,
that mirror's luffy's own appetite like none

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:23.370
other.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.319
Plus her face does look quite a lot like Luffy's.

00:17:27.319 --> 00:17:31.539
Bonnies saved Zoro from attacking a celestial
dragon, even though she could have easily

00:17:31.539 --> 00:17:36.669
not cared about the marines coming, and simply
disguised herself as a kid.

00:17:36.669 --> 00:17:43.320
We also know Bonnie has some ties to the revolutionary
army and dragon through Kuma, as we saw during

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:46.820
the reverie.

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:55.429
Kuma somehow knew about Luffy being Dragons
son before Ivankov.

00:17:55.429 --> 00:17:59.179
And it might be easy to think that she just
snuck into the holy land separately from the

00:17:59.179 --> 00:18:03.690
revolutionaries, but since she is there to
save Kuma, wouldn't it make way more sense

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:06.370
for her to have come with them?

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:10.389
There was also this weird situation with Blackbeard
and Akainu.

00:18:10.389 --> 00:18:16.980
On top of that, bonnie is inspired by the
most famous female pirate in history, Anne

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:23.029
Bonney, who escaped her execution, and was
reportedly pregnant at the time of her escape.

00:18:23.029 --> 00:18:29.779
Plus of course Bonnie and Clyde, which would
fit pretty damn well with her and dragon.

00:18:29.779 --> 00:18:35.669
Now, as promised, I'm gonna share my thoughts
and new insights on Crocomom with you as well.

00:18:35.669 --> 00:18:42.769
However since this video is already long enough
as is, Crocomom will get its own special video,

00:18:42.769 --> 00:18:48.279
that will be released 3 days from now, or
if you're from the future it's already here.

00:18:48.279 --> 00:18:59.250
Until then, I strongly recommend you check
out my video on Luffy's father dragon as well.

